S

#78002
"Wagon-Rutted Intersection"
"Broken barrels and splintered planks of wood litter the intersection of
paths here; their contants long looted and carted off.  The tops of
several tents peek out from behind the makeshift barricades all
throughout the camp.  The strong odor of unwashed bodies fills the air
and despite the stiff breeze blowing through the area the smell does not
fade.  To the north and south a small footpath has been cut through the
barricades.  To the east a dirt path proceeds deeper into the camp while
to the west it leads away from it.
"
""
