#78014
"Battery 'B' - Along a Row of Catapaults"
"Almost every bit of the ground along this strip of the footpath is
covered in the decaying corpses of goblins.  The stench of death is
overwhelming and many flies buzz around the dead bodies.  Large crates
line the edges of the footpath each containing cow's bladders filled with
a thick, oily substance.  Cut through the dirt barricade to the west is a
small opening leading into one of the catapault emplacements.  Dotting
the barren dirt landscape to the east and northeast you can see several
canvas tent tops peeking out above the barricades.  To the north and
south the footpath continues through the batteries of the camp.
"
""
