#78016
"Along a Cobblestone Wall"
"Built up about four feet high to the south is a crude cobblestone wall. 
Positioned in front of the wall are several rows of wooden spikes which
point out towards any incoming invaders.  Peering over the wall you
notice that just in front of the spikes a moat filled with a thick black
liquid has been dug.  The cobblestone wall continues to stretch out far
to the east as it runs along the outskirts of the camp.  To the north a
small dirt footpath makes its way through the crude dirt barricades.
"
""
