#78017
"Along a Cobblestone Wall"
"The blackened and charred remains of a tree lies directly in the center
of the path here; its twisted branches looking as though they could break
free at any time.  Atop the cobblestone wall which has been built along
the southern edge of the camp are several small humanoid skulls; each
covered in large spots of dried blood.  Bits and pieces of bone lie
scattered about the dark soil as well as a few pieces of decomposing
flesh.  Directly to the north a large dirt mound has been built up
concealing what lies in that direction.  The path continues along the
edge of the wall to the east and west from here.
"
""
